      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00056",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[56]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5190,
      "endIndex": 5282,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Premium shirts deserve proper care. Follow these steps, and they will look sharp for years.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00057",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[57]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5282,
      "endIndex": 5283,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00058",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[58]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5283,
      "endIndex": 5430,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "1. Wash on Cold: Heat is the enemy of natural fibers. Wash your shirts in cold water to completely avoid shrinkage and protect the vibrant colors.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00059",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[59]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5430,
      "endIndex": 5608,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "2. Button Them Up: Before throwing them in the machine, button the shirt up and turn it inside out. This protects the buttons from chipping and the collar from losing its shape.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00060",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[60]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5608,
      "endIndex": 5740,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "3. Ditch the Dryer: Never tumble dry your cotton and linen shirts. Hang them up on a good hanger and let them air dry in the shade.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00061",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[61]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5740,
      "endIndex": 5918,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "4. Ironing: Iron cotton shirts while they are still just a tiny bit damp. For linen, use a high heat setting with plenty of steam, or just embrace the natural, relaxed wrinkles!",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
